Question 4: Contradictions Between Any Sentences

Attack 1 (Trunkated text at LEDGER:17-18):

Claim in LEDGER:17-18: The note text for entry 10 ends abruptly mid-word: (agy walled until 2026- and line 18 is blank.

Comparison with other texts: SECTION:48-49 says "agy is walled until 2026-10-07 by its own message and the fix is one column." CHANGELOG:11-12 and MSG:3 say "Resets in 101h48m29s."

Finding: LEDGER:17-18 is an incomplete / truncated string ((agy walled until 2026-). In a commit ledger, a truncated JSON string field is malformed JSON or an incomplete entry note that must be completed prior to commit.

Attack 2 (Passage 2616 title / PPC reference in LEDGER:10):

LEDGER:10 states: #27 is a real gap -- qhppciphack carries its PPC half, qhm88kstops one MB89352 assignment of nine...

Neither SECTION nor CHANGELOG nor MSG mentions qhppciphack or the "PPC half" of passage 2616 (though LEDGER:4, 5, 6 refers to passage 2616 as '#12 m88k CMMU / dev_mb89352 fatal errors'). However, this is additional explanatory detail in the ledger entry note, not a direct contradiction.

Attack 3 (Astra passes count for table rows):

SECTION:50-51 states: "Astra's own passes read the whole table before #555 shipped (ifile_04: 128/128 rows)".

CHANGELOG:4 states: "#555 (c29a5fd3) was the largest records commit of the week -- 130 table rows...".

LEDGER:9 states: "Astra's ifile_04 (128/128 rows) and ifile_05 passes read them before #555 shipped."

CHANGELOG:4 mentions 130 table rows, while SECTION:50 and LEDGER:9 note ifile_04 had 128/128 rows. LEDGER:9 resolves this by noting both ifile_04 and ifile_05 passes covered them.

